tar","html_url":"https://github.com/ydeltastar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-12T12:53:45Z","updated_at":"2024-11-12T13:04:06Z","body":"> The problem is that it needs to apply only in game, not in the editor.\r\n\r\nProject settings should be applied in real-time in the editor so you can preview it and match runtime as closely as possible.\r\nYou can [override it](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/export/feature_tags.html#overriding-project-settings) for feature tags like `editor_runtime` and `release` if you want a setting to apply only in the running project.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470457085/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470560690","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98989#issuecomment-2470560690","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98989","id":2470560690,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TQcOy","user":{"login":"Summersay415","id":71974498,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxOTc0NDk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71974498?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415","html_url":"https://github.com/Summersay415","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-12T13:41:17Z","updated_at":"2024-11-12T13:41:17Z","body":"> > The problem is that it needs to apply only in game, not in the editor.\n> \n> Project settings should be applied in real-time in the editor so you can preview it and match runtime as closely as possible.\n> You can [override it](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/export/feature_tags.html#overriding-project-settings) for feature tags like `editor_runtime` and `release` if you want a setting to apply only in the running project.\n\nGood idea!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470560690/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2478270327","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98989#issuecomment-2478270327","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98989","id":2478270327,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Tt2d3","user":{"login":"Summersay415","id":71974498,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxOTc0NDk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71974498?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415","html_url":"https://github.com/Summersay415","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-15T08:57:19Z","updated_at":"2024-11-20T04:51:48Z","body":"> > The problem is that it needs to apply only in game, not in the editor.\r\n> \r\n> Project settings should be applied in real-time in the editor so you can preview it and match runtime as closely as possible. You can [override it](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/export/feature_tags.html#overriding-project-settings) for feature tags like `editor_runtime` and `release` if you want a setting to apply only in the running project.\r\n\r\nI looked into this variant and found that it will be very non-user-friendly: to run only in game you will need 3 settings (one for editor, another for editor_runtime and one more without feature tag). So, this way it will be implemented very strangely. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2478270327/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"resolved"}}]